racter message used as an acknowledgement (ACK), meaning \"previous message received and understood.\""],"glosses":["A single character message used as an acknowledgement (ACK), meaning \"previous message received and understood.\""],"id":"62eabb1a-7234-4679-a55b-dec1c6128fc5"},{"categories":["English abbreviations"],"links":[["go ahead","go ahead#English"],["over","over#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(Morse code) Abbreviation of go ahead, over, an indication that a message is complete and a reply is awaited."],"qualifier":"Morse code","glosses":["Abbreviation of go ahead, over, an indication that a message is complete and a reply is awaited."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"go ahead","extra":"an indication that a message is complete and a reply is awaited"},{"word":"over","extra":"an indication that a message is complete and a reply is awaited"}],"id":"bd48f03f-9873-4d28-8e64-b76aad76d47e"},{"topics":["ball-games","baseball","games","hobbies","lifestyle","sports"],"senseid":["en:strikeout"],"categories":["English abbreviations","en:Baseball"],"links":[["baseball","baseball"],["strikeout","strikeout#English"],["scorecard","scorecard#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(baseball) Abbreviation of strikeout On a baseball scorecard, a frontwards K signifies striking out while swinging the bat, while a backwards K signifies striking out while looking."],"glosses":["Abbreviation of strikeout On a baseball scorecard, a frontwards K signifies striking out while swinging the bat, while a backwards K signifies striking out while looking."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"strikeout On a baseball scorecard","extra":"a frontwards K signifies striking out while swinging the bat, while a backwards K signifies striking out while looking"}],"id":"9d0da08d-839f-4568-8016-69bf8f942093"},{"examples":[{"text":"1.e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. d4 exd4 4. e5 Ne4 5. Qxd4 d5 6. exd6 e.p. Nxd6 7. Bg5 Nc6 8. Qe3+ Be7 9. Nbd2 0-0 10. 0-0-0 Re8 11. Kb1 (=)","ref":"2022, “2023 Laws of Chess”, in FIDE, page 23:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[122,123]],"id":"05417580-cdfc-4499-b605-abbd7efb71ff"},{"text":"The correct answer is 1.Rxf6 Rxf6 2.Rf1 Raf8 3.Qg5 Kg7 4.Nh5+\nOther sub-variations work, such as playing 2.Qg5 then 3.Rf1 or playing 4.Bxf6+ first before playing 5.Nh5+.","ref":"2023 August 12, GM Noël Studer, “Mastering Chess Puzzles: The Comprehensive Guide to Effective Problem Solving”, in Next Level Chess:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[51,52]],"id":"fcc2b20f-eb3b-4636-8778-05e0ff2df250"}],"topics":["board-games","card-games","chess","games"],"categories":["English abbreviations","English terms with quotations","en:Card games","en:Chess"],"links":[["card game","card game"],["chess","chess"],["king","king#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(card games, chess) Abbreviation of king."],"glosses":["Abbreviation of king."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"king"}],"id":"404a5e19-a67f-4d56-80b3-daefe634076d"},{"topics":["biology","natural-sciences"],"categories":["English abbreviations","en:Biology"],"links":[["biology","biology"],["carrying capacity","carrying capacity#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(biology) Abbreviation of carrying capacity."],"glosses":["Abbreviation of carrying capacity."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"carrying capacity"}],"id":"74051683-377e-4956-954a-d2c8aba8a0b9"},{"topics":["geography","geology","natural-sciences"],"categories":["English abbreviations","en:Geology"],"links":[["geology","geology"],["Cretaceous","Cretaceous#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(geology) Abbreviation of Cretaceous."],"glosses":["Abbreviation of Cretaceous."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of"],"alt_of":[{"word":"Cretaceous"}],"id":"a3af4df0-5359-43a8-a4c9-600bf171808b"},{"examples":[{"text":"Knit 3, p 1, k 2, purl 1, k 2, m 1, k 2 together, k 1.","ref":"1855, Godey's Magazine, volume 51, page 71:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[13,14],[26,27],[36,37],[50,51]],"id":"c2e35fae-7366-4adc-9f91-d